  "title": "Bridge Pact",
  "rules": [
    "Four builders start with complementary finite wood and bolts on opposite islands. Two distinct three-cell crossing routes exist at y=1 and y=5.",
    "A cell requires one wood and one bolts, committed from the cell or a cardinal neighbor. Same-material contention awards the lowest agent id; complementary contributions combine simultaneously.",
    "Newly complete cells receive integrity twelve. Old complete cells with positive integrity admit one builder per cell; old occupied destinations block swaps.",
    "Every entry causes one wear and every fourth transition causes one decay. Zero integrity blocks new entry but never moves or removes an existing occupant.",
    "Repair consumes one wood and one bolts, restores six integrity up to twelve, and may restore a worn-out occupied cell. Adjacent peers may transfer one material.",
    "Private destination values permit different route priorities. AUTHOR SOURCE ONLY: no connectivity trace, successful crossing, animation, causality test or learning result has been executed."
  ],
